# shir_nodes/cut_at.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# CutAt: cut `text` at ONE occurrence of `delim` — the four single-star
# glob-strip identities that are pure find()/rfind() work:
#
#   ${v%%lit*}   keep the head BEFORE the first  occurrence  (head,  first)
#   ${v%lit*}    keep the head BEFORE the last   occurrence  (head,  !first)
#   ${v#*lit}    keep the tail AFTER  the first  occurrence  (!head, first)
#   ${v##*lit}   keep the tail AFTER  the last   occurrence  (!head, !first)
#
# No match leaves the text unchanged (bash's strip is a no-op when the
# pattern does not match). `delim` is a magic-free literal (the fold
# refuses `*`/`?`/`[`/`\` bodies), so the glob engine is never needed —
# each identity follows from glob semantics: `*` matches the empty
# string, shortest-vs-longest picks the cut point. Verified against bash
# (match / no-match / empty-delim / multi-byte literal cases) before the
# node was written; see transforms/affix_strip_fold.rs's module doc.
#
# Emitted by the `affix-strip-fold` transform (the star-form branch; the
# plain-literal branch keeps using AffixStrip).
#
# Backends: Rust (find/rfind + slicing), C (one strstr find + a vbuf
#   copy — see c_backend's ext_value_c CutAt arm) — target-gated offers;
#   other backends accept by adding a render arm and their target to the
#   gate (the FieldGrab offer pattern).
# Fallback: sh2.cutAt(text, delim, head, first)

node CutAt
tag "CutAt"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field text: expr
field delim: string
field head: bool
field first: bool
spec: none (unstated)
